One definition of a player's dungeon role, used by every part of LFG.
Touches: modules/mod-playerbots/src/Bot/PlayerbotAI.cpp and .h (new
PlayerbotAI::GetDungeonRole, plus the DK case of IsTank),
modules/mod-playerbots/src/Bot/RandomPlayerbotMgr.cpp (LfgFillRoleOf),
modules/mod-playerbots/src/Ai/Base/Actions/LfgActions.cpp (LfgJoinAction::GetRoles)
Applies on top of 0016-playerbot-lfg-fill-roles.core-patch.

Why: reported as "bots still aren't being generated with the correct specs for
the roles they should be using -- keep getting healers marked as dps or dps
marked as healers and everyone dies".

The same feature answered "what role is this player" two different ways, and
they disagreed:

  * LfgJoinAction::GetRoles -- what a bot QUEUES as -- was a per-class switch on
    the talent tab, written out longhand, with a second and different path for
    non-random bots.
  * LfgFillRoleOf -- what the group fill COUNTS, what RespecBotForRole verifies
    against, and what lands on the party-frame role icon via Group::AddMember --
    called PlayerbotAI::IsTank/IsHeal with bySpec defaulted to false, which asks
    the bot's ACTIVE AI STRATEGY.

Talents and strategies are only in step immediately after botAI->Reset(); a bot
that was respecced, randomised or re-targeted since then reports one role and
plays the other. A bot could queue as a healer and be counted as dps -- so the
fill added a second healer and no tank -- or queue as dps and be counted as the
healer, which is the group with no healer at all.

Three narrower bugs fell out of the same tangle:

  * IsTank(player, bySpec = true) returned true for ANY death knight standing in
    Frost Presence, not just blood. Real players have no bot AI, so they always
    take the bySpec path: a frost dps in the group was counted as its tank and
    the fill then added no tank. Now blood tab only.
  * The feral druid tank/cat call was made differently in each place (one asked
    for the Thick Hide aura, the other for bear form right now). It is now made
    exactly the way AiFactory::AddDefaultCombatStrategies makes it -- cat when
    the druid has Cat Form and no Thick Hide, bear otherwise -- so the role and
    the behaviour cannot disagree.
  * A ret paladin running the optional "offheal" strategy reports as a healer,
    because OffhealRetPaladinStrategy carries STRATEGY_TYPE_HEAL. That is
    correct for the strategy and wrong for a role, and it is unreachable now
    that roles never consult strategies. Latent rather than live -- offheal is
    opt-in via `co +offheal` and is not in AiFactory's defaults -- but it is the
    same class of bug and it is closed by the same change.

GetDungeonRole reads the talent tab and nothing else: no shapeshift form, no
presence, no strategy. Those describe what someone is doing this second, and an
LFG role has to be answerable for a bot standing in a city out of form with its
AI not yet built, and for a real player, who has no bot AI at all.

--- a/modules/mod-playerbots/src/Bot/PlayerbotAI.h
+++ b/modules/mod-playerbots/src/Bot/PlayerbotAI.h
@@
     static bool IsDps(Player* player, bool bySpec = false);
+    // The one answer to "which of the three roles does this player fill in a
+    // dungeon". Returns an lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_* bit. See the definition.
+    static uint8 GetDungeonRole(Player* player);

--- a/modules/mod-playerbots/src/Bot/PlayerbotAI.cpp
+++ b/modules/mod-playerbots/src/Bot/PlayerbotAI.cpp
@@ (above IsTank)
+uint8 PlayerbotAI::GetDungeonRole(Player* player)
+{
+    constexpr uint32 DRUID_CAT_FORM = 768;
+    constexpr uint32 DRUID_THICK_HIDE = 16931;
+
+    if (!player)
+        return lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_DAMAGE;
+
+    uint8 const tab = AiFactory::GetPlayerSpecTab(player);
+    switch (player->getClass())
+    {
+        case CLASS_WARRIOR:
+            return tab == WARRIOR_TAB_PROTECTION ? lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_TANK : lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_DAMAGE;
+        case CLASS_DEATH_KNIGHT:
+            return tab == DEATH_KNIGHT_TAB_BLOOD ? lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_TANK : lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_DAMAGE;
+        case CLASS_PALADIN:
+            if (tab == PALADIN_TAB_PROTECTION)
+                return lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_TANK;
+            return tab == PALADIN_TAB_HOLY ? lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_HEALER : lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_DAMAGE;
+        case CLASS_DRUID:
+            if (tab == DRUID_TAB_RESTORATION)
+                return lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_HEALER;
+            if (tab == DRUID_TAB_FERAL
+                && !(player->HasSpell(DRUID_CAT_FORM) && !player->HasAura(DRUID_THICK_HIDE)))
+                return lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_TANK;
+            return lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_DAMAGE;
+        case CLASS_PRIEST:
+            return tab == PRIEST_TAB_SHADOW ? lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_DAMAGE : lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_HEALER;
+        case CLASS_SHAMAN:
+            return tab == SHAMAN_TAB_RESTORATION ? lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_HEALER : lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_DAMAGE;
+        default:
+            return lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_DAMAGE;
+    }
+}
+
 bool PlayerbotAI::IsTank(Player* player, bool bySpec)
@@ (IsTank, death knight case)
         case CLASS_DEATH_KNIGHT:
-            if (tab == DEATH_KNIGHT_TAB_BLOOD || player->HasAura(SPELL_DK_FROST_PRESENCE))
+            // Blood only -- see the patch note about frost dps being counted
+            // as a group's tank.
+            if (tab == DEATH_KNIGHT_TAB_BLOOD)
             {
                 return true;
             }
             break;

--- a/modules/mod-playerbots/src/Bot/RandomPlayerbotMgr.cpp
+++ b/modules/mod-playerbots/src/Bot/RandomPlayerbotMgr.cpp
@@ (LfgFillRoleOf, from 0016)
 static uint8 LfgFillRoleOf(Player* player)
 {
-    if (PlayerbotAI::IsTank(player))
-        return lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_TANK;
-
-    if (PlayerbotAI::IsHeal(player))
-        return lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_HEALER;
-
-    return lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_DAMAGE;
+    return PlayerbotAI::GetDungeonRole(player);
 }

--- a/modules/mod-playerbots/src/Ai/Base/Actions/LfgActions.cpp
+++ b/modules/mod-playerbots/src/Ai/Base/Actions/LfgActions.cpp
@@ (LfgJoinAction::GetRoles -- the whole per-class switch is replaced)
 uint32 LfgJoinAction::GetRoles()
 {
-    if (!RandomPlayerbotMgr::instance().IsRandomBot(bot))
-    {
-        if (botAI->IsTank(bot))
-            return PLAYER_ROLE_TANK;
-        ...
-    }
-
-    uint8 spec = AiFactory::GetPlayerSpecTab(bot);
-    switch (bot->getClass())
-    {
-        ... 50 lines of per-class tab tests ...
-    }
-
-    return PLAYER_ROLE_DAMAGE;
+    return PlayerbotAI::GetDungeonRole(bot);
 }
